*** Provenance -- not a legal notice ***

Recorded so a known gap in the chain of title is not discovered late.

The immediate parent of this module is ADTucsen
(https://github.com/djvine/ADTucsen) by David Vine, whose driver header states it
was "Based on Mark Rivers PointGrey driver" -- hence the areaDetector notice
above. **The ADTucsen repository itself ships no LICENSE file**, which by default
leaves David Vine's own contributions all-rights-reserved rather than explicitly
licensed.

Recommended: ask David Vine to add a licence to ADTucsen, or to confirm in
writing that the EPICS Open License applies to it. One email removes the
ambiguity permanently.

The Tucsen TUCam SDK this module links against is proprietary vendor material
under Tucsen's own terms and is NOT covered by any licence in this file. This
repository contains no copy of it; it is obtained from Tucsen
(https://www.tucsen.com/download-software/) and installed system-wide -- see
README.md, "The TUCam SDK dependency".
